      "latency_ms": 2262.6,
      "prompt_tokens": 11,
      "completion_tokens": 517,
      "output": "At its most basic level, **water** is a chemical compound made of hydrogen and oxygen. It is the most abundant molecule on Earth's surface and is essential for all known forms of life. \n\nHere is a breakdown of water, explained through different lenses:\n\n### 1. The Chemical View\n* **Chemical Formula:** $\\text{H}_2\\text{O}$\n* **Composition:** Each molecule of water is made up of **two hydrogen atoms** bonded to **one oxygen atom**.\n* **States of Matter:** Water is unique because it is the only natural substance on Earth that exists abundantly in three physical states:\n  * **Liquid** (water in oceans, rivers, rain)\n  * **Solid** (ice, snow, glaciers)\n  * **Gas** (water vapor, steam, humidity)\n\n### 2. Physical Properties\nWater has several remarkable properties that make it unique and vital to the universe:\n* **The \"Universal Solvent\":** Water can dissolve more substances than any other liquid. This is how it carries nutrients and minerals through our bodies and through the soil.\n* **Cohesion and Adhesion:** Water molecules like to stick to each other (cohesion—which creates surface tension, allowing some bugs to walk on water) and to other surfaces (adhesion—which helps water move up the roots of tall trees).\n* **Density Anomaly:** Most substances shrink and become denser when they freeze. Water, however, **expands and becomes less dense** when it turns to ice. This is why ice floats, which prevents lakes and oceans from freezing solid from the bottom up, allowing marine life to survive the winter.\n* **High Heat Capacity:** Water can absorb a lot of heat before its temperature changes significantly. This helps regulate the climate of the entire planet and keeps our bodies from overheating.\n\n### 3. Ecological and Biological Importance\n* **The Engine of Life:** All living things—from tiny bacteria to giant blue whales—are mostly made of water (humans are about 60% water). It regulates body temperature, lubricates joints, and flushes out waste.\n* **Earth's Life Support:** About **71% of Earth's surface** is covered in water, mostly in oceans. It drives weather patterns, shapes continents, and creates the climates necessary for ecosystems to thrive.\n\n### Summary\nIn short, water is a simple molecule with extraordinary properties. Without it, life as we know it simply could not exist."
